//  libs/aocnet/tests/test_repl_vendor.cpp
//
//  Plan E1, stage 1: the vendor RPCs (protocol/repl/vendor_codec.h and vendor_rpc.h) against what the retail client and server sent
//  (tests/capture_vendor.h, generated by tools/capture/gen_vendor.py).
//
//    * ServerInteractWithInteractableComponent (capture 716), ServerHandleVendorPurchase (863: one item, 1531: one item with an optional set,
//      1536: six items), ServerHandleVendorTransaction (716: a sale) and ClientOpenVendor (716): each read to its last bit with the schema
//      entry of its RPC, parsed into its typed form, built again from the typed form and written: the same bits.
//    * What each call holds (the vendor guid of the captures, the items and quantities, the optional that is set).
//    * ServerGetNodeTaxTable and the server's ClientSetNodeTaxTable (716, 1536; fix 4): the table the vendor window waits for, 78 entries and
//      6,817 bytes each, read, typed (FNodeTaxDetails: the node, the tags, the records and the values), written back to the same bits.
//    * The limits: a cart of 255 items round-trips, one of 256 is refused by the writer; a negative count, a count the bits cannot hold and
//      an optional flag above 1 are refused by the reader.
//    * Hostile input: every truncation of every captured call, and a seeded fuzz of them (bit flips, cuts, noise tails), each read from a
//      heap buffer of exactly the bytes it needs: nothing crashes, and whatever reads writes back to a payload that reads equal.
// ============================================================================
